  "body": "I am not sure what to call this, but I am running a Synapse homeserver, installed with the default [Beeper self-hosted instructions](https://github.com/beeper/self-host/blob/dc95f18826cb0d4cfd204fc5ae4db1094f6495c9/README.md#self-host-install-guide), in other words almost a basic Ansible playbook.\r\n\r\nThe thing I am experiencing is I for example start a chat in Discord though any app (but in this case testing element), it works well, then suddenly it starts to open new chats with that person, that also got a matrix account, making the messages to be duplicated through more than one \"channel\". Is it possible to stop this behavior?\r\n\r\nIn the app this is auto-made: \"Tony and one other were invited and joined\", so I have to manually leave those chats to not get duplicate messages.\r\n",
